{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 46, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the sunlight too bright, the colors too saturated. He sat up in bed, a strange metallic scent filling his nostrils. His room wasn't his room. It was…cleaner. Too clean. The furniture was pristine, the posters on the wall depicting fantastical landscapes he’d only seen in RPGs. A notification popped up in his vision, a translucent overlay on reality: \"Welcome, Player 472! Level 1 achieved. Quest: Retrieve the Sunstone from the Goblin Caves.\" He reached out, his hand phasing slightly through the bedside table. Panic seized him. This wasn't a dream. This was…real? Or unreal? He felt a strange surge of power, a sense of potential he’d never experienced before. A quest? He was in a video game.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of bed, the floor feeling oddly responsive beneath his feet. He found a simple tunic and trousers laid out on a chair, and as he donned them, a stat panel appeared in his peripheral vision: Strength: 10, Dexterity: 8, Intelligence: 12. He was a character, a player in someone else's world. The door to his room swung open, revealing a woman with impossibly long, flowing hair and eyes the color of amethyst. \"Greetings, Arthur,\" she said, her voice like wind chimes. \"I am Elara, your guide. The fate of Eldoria rests upon your shoulders.\" He swallowed, trying to process the information. Goblin Caves? Sunstone? This was insane. But as he looked at his reflection in a polished shield leaning against the wall, a flicker of something akin to excitement sparked within him. He had a quest. He had a purpose. He had a game to play.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.18361379206180573}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.32705190777778625}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0002044230350293219}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.10078337788581848}, {"token": "▁sunlight", "logprob": -1.43425714969635}, {"token": "▁too", "l